Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:58:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 27/31] drm/amd/display: APPLE5K log lines for iMac20 bring-up
 (A8)

The reference stack already logs the stitch decisions (TILED_STITCH:) and
link health (APPLE5K: link-health). Add the three things a test rig
needs on the iMac20 that it does not yet say, all only on a DMI-matched
iMac20:

 - at DM init, which tiled_stitch and tiled_genlock values are in force;
 - when the pair is wired, which link indices it pairs (checks A2);
 - after each settle pass, which OTG drives each tile, which genlock mode
   ran, and the measured phase between them in lines. This is at info
   level while a post-modeset link-health sequence is armed and at debug
   level afterwards, so page flips do not flood the log.

The pair lookup in amdgpu_dm_tiled_measured_realign() moves into
amdgpu_dm_tiled_find_pair() so both callers share it. No behaviour change.

[adapter: new, Sysadmin patches/amdgpu-imac20-2-5k-stitch DESIGN.md A8]

